---
/**
 * /settings: the one machinery page. Three sections, in order: Account (name,
 * email, resume email and handle, each a collapsed row that opens to its own
 * form, see AccountRow.astro), Models and keys (the drafting toggle plus one
 * unified row per provider combining its key and its writing model, see
 * ProviderRows.astro), and Your data (download or delete). It reads as the
 * same collapsed-row system the profile page uses: a setting is a fact with an
 * edit behind it, not a form standing open.
 *
 * WHY THIS IS ONE FILE, NOT THREE. It used to be three pages: /account/
 * settings (name, email, handle, the draft-on-apply toggle), /account/keys
 * (the four provider-key panels), and /account (download and delete, plus a
 * "your surfaces" hub the shared header and footer now cover on their own).
 * A person turning drafting on and a person connecting the key that powers
 * it were one errand split across two pages for no reason but history; this
 * merge puts the toggle and the four provider panels in the same "Drafting"
 * section so the sentence "turn this on, then connect a key" reads as one
 * panel instead of a cross-link. The old /account hub's "your surfaces" nav
 * is gone with it: that job now belongs to the shared chrome and to Profile,
 * not to a page that also has to explain how to delete your account.
 *
 * GATED BY THE '/settings' PREFIX IN src/lib/entitlement.ts, COVERING THIS
 * PAGE AND EVERY ENDPOINT UNDER IT BY PREFIX MATCH. No second ROUTE_POLICY
 * entry is needed for settings/name.ts, settings/email.ts, settings/
 * handle.ts, settings/generation.ts, settings/keys/save.ts, settings/keys/
 * remove.ts, settings/export.ts, or settings/delete.ts: they all live under
 * this one tree specifically so entitlement.ts needs one policy entry, not
 * eight.
 *
 * WORKS WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT. Every form here is a plain POST to its own
 * endpoint, redirecting back to this page with a query param this
 * frontmatter reads to decide which message to show. The one script on this
 * page (at the bottom) only makes the delete disclosure's Cancel button
 * close it without a round trip; the disclosure closes exactly the same way
 * with the script absent, by clicking its own summary again or tabbing away.
 *
 * WHY EMAIL AND NAME ARE TWO FORMS, NOT ONE. They post to two different
 * endpoints with two entirely different failure shapes (name always
 * succeeds or reveals a broken profile row; email starts a two-step
 * confirmation Better Auth owns and can fail for session freshness, an
 * unchanged address, or a disabled feature), so one submit button doing
 * both would have to explain which of two unrelated things went wrong from
 * one message. Two forms, two plain results.
 *
 * WHAT "REQUESTED" HONESTLY MEANS FOR EMAIL. This page never claims an
 * email change has happened, because from this route's point of view it has
 * not: see src/pages/settings/email.ts's own header for the full two-step
 * sequence, verified against Better Auth's source rather than assumed. The
 * copy below says "a confirmation is on its way to CURRENT ADDRESS", not
 * "your email is changing", and names the address the confirmation goes to
 * so a reader knows which inbox to check.
 *
 * THE HANDLE PANEL, MASTER-SPEC F8. This is where a person picks the value
 * src/pages/u/[handle].astro later checks ownership against. Not the same
 * discipline as the name panel above: RUN-FINISH 2.1's verbatim-storage
 * rule is about a NAME, and a handle is a constrained-alphabet identifier,
 * not free text someone is being quoted back. What this panel says about
 * visibility is scoped to what is actually true today: RUN-MASTER
 * amendment 6 keeps every classification above private dark this run, so
 * the copy below says the handle is a private preview only its owner can
 * open, not a promise about who can see it later.
 *
 * THE DRAFTING SECTION, FOLDED FROM TWO PAGES INTO ONE PANEL. The toggle
 * writes db/011_generation_on_apply.sql's generate_on_apply column through
 * src/lib/generation-preference-store.ts (getGenerationPreference() here,
 * settings/generation.ts on write); turning it on does not, by itself,
 * generate anything, and the copy says so, because it is one of four gates
 * src/lib/generation-preference.ts's decideGenerationTrigger() checks, never
 * a trigger by itself. THE COVENANT THIS PANEL DOES NOT TOUCH: nothing
 * about this setting ever marks a click "applied"; see src/pages/desk/
 * application.ts's own header for where that line is actually enforced.
 * Below the toggle, one add-a-key form and a table of the keys already on
 * file. The form is a provider dropdown (src/lib/keychain.ts PROVIDERS,
 * labeled from src/lib/generation-providers.ts's PROVIDER_REGISTRY, the
 * canonical names generation actually calls by, e.g. "Kimi (Moonshot AI)",
 * not a second, locally-invented label map) and the key field itself. The
 * table shows one row per connected provider: the provider, the last 4
 * characters and the two dates keyMeta() returns (never the key itself), and a
 * Remove control.
 * One key per provider (db/007's primary key), so saving a provider already
 * in the table replaces its key rather than adding a second row.
 *
 * THREE WAYS THE KEY PANELS REFUSE TO SHOW A FORM, AND ONLY TWO OF THEM
 * STILL BLOCK ANYTHING HERE. keys.astro used to refuse for three reasons:
 * not signed in, the `byok` flag off, or KEY_ENCRYPTION_SECRET unset. The
 * first of those is now the whole page's own gate below (a signed-out
 * reader never reaches the Drafting section, or any other section, because
 * none of them exist without a session). The other two are real states a
 * signed-in reader can be in, so they render as a quiet note inside this
 * one section instead of hiding the rest of the page: a person whose
 * deployment has byok off, or whose operator has not set an encryption
 * secret, still gets to change their name, their email, their handle, and
 * still gets to download or delete their data.
 *
 * ROUTES ARE WRITTEN THROUGH routeFor(), NOT withBase(), FOR EVERY FORM
 * ACTION AND LINK BELOW EXCEPT THE HANDLE PREVIEW. Every endpoint this page
 * points at (settings-name, settings-email, settings-handle, settings-
 * generation, settings-keys-save, settings-keys-remove, settings-export,
 * settings-delete) and the cross-link to Profile are registered static
 * ROUTES entries in src/data/nav.ts, so routeFor() is what builds their
 * paths. The one exception is the handle preview link, /u/<handle>: that is
 * a dynamic route (src/pages/u/[handle].astro, key 'account-handle'), and
 * routeFor() refuses to build a dynamic route on purpose, so this page
 * calls withBase() directly for that one href, matching the parameterised
 * paths jobPath() and killCardPath() build the same way.
 *
 * HOW A FAILED KEY SUBMISSION GETS BACK HERE. A 303 redirect carries no
 * body, so settings/keys/save.ts and settings/keys/remove.ts relay the
 * outcome through a short-lived, httpOnly cookie, the same technique
 * record.astro's own relay uses. THE SUBMITTED KEY IS NEVER PART OF THAT
 * PAYLOAD: the relay carries only which provider and what was wrong, in
 * words, never the value that was typed. See the password field below for
 * the other half of that same rule.
 *
 * THE DELETE DISCLOSURE, FOLDED IN FROM THE OLD /account HUB. A native
 * <details>/<summary> needs no script to open, trap focus, or close, and is
 * exactly as keyboard-operable as a link. The first click (on <summary>) is
 * step one of the two-step confirmation: it reveals exactly what gets
 * erased and what does not before the second, destructive control is
 * anywhere on screen. The delete form itself is a plain POST; see
 * src/pages/settings/delete.ts's own header for why that route accepts a
 * native form submission with no script required for the action to work.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import ProviderRows from '../components/settings/ProviderRows.astro';
import { isPaidViewer } from '../lib/ledger-access';
import AccountRow from '../components/settings/AccountRow.astro';
import { routeFor } from '../data/nav';
import { withBase } from '../../site.config.mjs';
import { getHandle, getResumeEmailSettings, personName, HANDLE_MAX_LENGTH, HANDLE_MIN_LENGTH } from '../lib/record-store';
import { getGenerationPreference } from '../lib/generation-preference-store';
import { getAuth } from '../lib/auth';
import { isOn } from '../lib/flags';
import { PROVIDERS, keyStorageIsConfigured, type Provider } from '../lib/keychain';
import { getWritingModel, keyMeta, type StoredKeyMeta } from '../lib/keychain-store';
import { sumUserRenderUsage } from '../lib/generated-render-store';
import { estimateDraftCost, formatCost, PRICES_AS_OF } from '../lib/generation-cost';
import { PROVIDER_REGISTRY } from '../lib/generation-providers';

export const prerender = false;

const verdict = Astro.locals.verdict;
const allowed = verdict?.allow === true;
const reason = verdict?.reason ?? 'signed-out';
const viewer = Astro.locals.viewer;

const name = allowed && viewer ? await personName(viewer.userId) : null;
// See settings/email.ts's own header for why the email address has no
// reader through record-store.ts: Better Auth owns `user.email` and this is
// the one place inside this page's frontmatter that asks it directly.
const session = allowed ? await getAuth().api.getSession({ headers: Astro.request.headers }) : null;
const email = session?.user?.email ?? null;
const handle = allowed && viewer ? await getHandle(viewer.userId) : null;
const generateOnApply = allowed && viewer ? await getGenerationPreference(viewer.userId) : false;

// Drafting spend so far (db/203): the person's own token usage summed per
// provider/model, priced by the dated table (generation-cost.ts). Only renders
// that measured usage count; a deterministic no-key draft billed nothing.
const usageGroups = allowed && viewer ? await sumUserRenderUsage(viewer.userId) : [];
let draftUsd = 0;
let draftCount = 0;
let draftTokens = 0;
for (const g of usageGroups) {
  draftCount += g.drafts;
  draftTokens += g.inputTokens + g.outputTokens;
  const est = estimateDraftCost({ provider: g.provider, model: g.model, inputTokens: g.inputTokens, outputTokens: g.outputTokens });
  if (est) draftUsd += est.usd;
}
const hasDraftSpend = draftCount > 0;
const draftSpendText = formatCost(draftUsd);
const draftTokensText = draftTokens >= 1000 ? `${Math.round(draftTokens / 100) / 10}k` : String(draftTokens);
const resumeEmail = allowed && viewer ? await getResumeEmailSettings(viewer.userId) : { useLogin: true, custom: null };

// The two key-panel refusal states that still matter once a reader has
// already cleared the page-level gate above; see this file's own header for
// why "not signed in" is no longer a third state checked here.
/* Bring-your-own-key is paid (the tiers matrix marks it N, N, Y), and the key
   exists to draft, which is paid too. A member who is not paying was able to
   connect one here and be billed by their provider for a feature the account
   does not carry, so the whole panel needs the tier (owner, 2026-09-21). */
const paidViewer = isPaidViewer(viewer);
const byokOn = isOn('byok');
const keysReady = allowed && byokOn;
const keysConfigured = keysReady ? keyStorageIsConfigured() : false;

const params = Astro.url.searchParams;
const nameUpdated = params.has('name-updated');
const nameError = params.has('name-error');
const emailRequested = params.has('email-requested');
const emailError = params.get('email-error');
const resumeEmailUpdated = params.has('resume-email-updated');
const resumeEmailError = params.has('resume-email-error');
const handleUpdated = params.has('handle-updated');
const handleCleared = params.has('handle-cleared');
const handleError = params.get('handle-error');
const generationUpdated = params.has('generation-updated');
const generationError = params.has('generation-error');
const modelUpdated = params.has('model-updated');
const modelError = params.has('model-error');
const deleteFailed = params.has('delete-failed');

const EMAIL_ERROR_MESSAGES: Record<string, string> = {
  empty: 'Type the new address before submitting.',
  'stale-session':
    'This session has been open too long to change something this sensitive. Sign out and back in, then try again.',
  'request-failed':
    'The request did not go through. Check the address is different from your current one and looks like a real ' +
    'email, then try again.'
};

const HANDLE_ERROR_MESSAGES: Record<string, string> = {
  invalid: `Use ${HANDLE_MIN_LENGTH} to ${HANDLE_MAX_LENGTH} characters: lowercase letters, numbers and hyphens ` +
    'only, starting and ending with a letter or number.',
  taken: 'That handle is already taken. Try another; nothing about your account has changed.',
  'no-profile': 'That did not save. Nothing has changed; try again, and if it keeps failing, contact ' +
    'ryan@tokenstoagents.ai.'
};

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The keys relay cookie: what a failed add/replace carried back. Read once,
   then deleted, so a reload never repeats it. Never carries the submitted
   key, only which provider and a human-readable reason; see settings/keys/
   save.ts's own header for the write side.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

interface KeysRelay {
  provider: Provider;
  message: string;
}

function parseKeysRelay(raw: string | undefined): KeysRelay | null {
  if (!raw) return null;
  try {
    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw) as Partial<KeysRelay>;
    if (typeof parsed.provider === 'string' && (PROVIDERS as readonly string[]).includes(parsed.provider) && typeof parsed.message === 'string') {
      return parsed as KeysRelay;
    }
    return null;
  } catch {
    // A cookie that fails to parse is treated as absent, never as a thrown
    // error: it can only mean the cookie was tampered with or truncated,
    // and either way there is nothing here for this page to recover.
    return null;
  }
}

const RELAY_COOKIE_PATH = withBase('/settings');
const keysRelay = parseKeysRelay(Astro.cookies.get('keys_form_relay')?.value);
Astro.cookies.delete('keys_form_relay', { path: RELAY_COOKIE_PATH });

function formatDate(date: Date): string {
  const MONTH_NAMES = [
    'January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June',
    'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December'
  ] as const;
  return `${MONTH_NAMES[date.getUTCMonth()]} ${date.getUTCDate()}, ${date.getUTCFullYear()}`;
}

// Every provider this person has a key on file for, in one ordered list the
// keys table renders a row per. One key per provider by construction (db/007's
// PRIMARY KEY), so this doubles as "which providers are connected".
const connectedKeys: StoredKeyMeta[] = keysConfigured && viewer ? await keyMeta(viewer.userId) : [];

/**
 * The writing-model picker's rows: one per connected provider, carrying that
 * provider's own curated list and this person's current choice.
 *
 * The labels and notes come from PROVIDER_REGISTRY, never a second map typed
 * here: keys-page.render.test.ts already pins that regression for provider
 * names, and a model list invented locally would drift from the one the
 * drafting code actually calls.
 */
// One row per provider, keys and writing model unified the way the design mock
// draws them (see ProviderRows.astro). Every provider is listed, connected or
// not; a connected one carries its key facts, its chosen writing model, and the
// copy tier it reads with. All model facts come from PROVIDER_REGISTRY, so the
// list cannot drift from the one the drafting code calls.
const providerRows =
  keysConfigured && viewer
    ? await Promise.all(
        PROVIDERS.map(async (provider) => {
          const def = PROVIDER_REGISTRY[provider];
          const key = connectedKeys.find((row) => row.provider === provider) ?? null;
          const connected = key !== null;
          const chosen = connected
            ? ((await getWritingModel(viewer.userId, provider)) ?? def.defaultWritingModel)
            : def.defaultWritingModel;
          const chosenModel = def.writingModels.find((model) => model.id === chosen);
          // The copy tier is a raw id with no label of its own, but every
          // provider's copyModel also appears in its writingModels (the cheapest
          // tier is a writing option too), so its friendly name is read from
          // there, with the id as a fallback.
          const readModelLabel =
            def.writingModels.find((model) => model.id === def.copyModel)?.label ?? def.copyModel;
          return {
            provider,
            name: def.label,
            connected,
            tail: key?.last4 ?? null,
            added: key ? formatDate(key.createdAt) : null,
            replaced: key?.rotatedAt ? formatDate(key.rotatedAt) : null,
            writingLabel: connected ? (chosenModel?.label ?? chosen) : null,
            readModelLabel,
            models: def.writingModels.map((model) => ({
              id: model.id,
              label: model.label,
              note: model.note,
              current: model.id === chosen
            })),
            relayError: keysRelay?.provider === provider ? keysRelay.message : null
          };
        })
      )
    : [];

// When exactly one key is connected, the autodraft toggle can name the model a
// draft will actually use; with several, each provider carries its own choice
// and there is no single "active" one to name.
const connectedRows = providerRows.filter((row) => row.connected);
const soleWritingModel = connectedRows.length === 1 ? connectedRows[0] : null;

// Which provider row is expanded, read from the query the row's own action
// links set: `?model=<provider>` opens its writing-model picker, `?connect=
// <provider>` opens its key field. Validated against the real provider list so
// a hand-typed value opens nothing. ProviderRows also opens a key row on its
// own relay error, independent of these.
const settingsPath = routeFor('settings');
const openModelParam = params.get('model');
const openConnectParam = params.get('connect');
const openModel = providerRows.some((row) => row.provider === openModelParam) ? openModelParam : null;
const openKey = providerRows.some((row) => row.provider === openConnectParam) ? openConnectParam : null;

const nameAction = routeFor('settings-name');
const emailAction = routeFor('settings-email');
const resumeEmailAction = routeFor('settings-resume-email');
const handleAction = routeFor('settings-handle');
const generationAction = routeFor('settings-generation');
const modelAction = routeFor('settings-model');
const keysSaveAction = routeFor('settings-keys-save');
const keysRemoveAction = routeFor('settings-keys-remove');
const exportHref = routeFor('settings-export');
const deleteAction = routeFor('settings-delete');
const profileHref = routeFor('profile');

/* The collapsed-row values and open states for the Account section. A row
   opens when its own save just happened, so its message and its form are both
   in view on the reload. */
const fullName = name && (name.firstName || name.lastName) ? `${name.firstName} ${name.lastName}`.trim() : 'Not set';
const resumeEmailValue = resumeEmail.useLogin
  ? 'Same as your login email'
  : (resumeEmail.custom ?? 'Not set');
const handleValue = handle ? `/u/${handle}` : 'Not set';
const nameRowOpen = nameUpdated || nameError;
const emailRowOpen = emailRequested || Boolean(emailError);
const resumeEmailRowOpen = resumeEmailUpdated || resumeEmailError;
const handleRowOpen = handleUpdated || handleCleared || Boolean(handleError);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Settings"
  description="Name, email, handle, drafting with provider keys, and download or delete your data."
  noindex
>
  <section class="settings-page">
    <div class="shell settings-shell">
      <span class="kicker">Account</span>

      {
        allowed ? (
          <>
            <h1>Settings</h1>

            <Panel title="Account" class="settings-panel">
              <AccountRow label="Name" value={fullName} open={nameRowOpen}>
                <p class="settings-panel-line">
                  Stored exactly as you type it: no capitalisation, no trimming, no cleanup of any kind. This
                  is the name every outreach draft and every generated document uses.
                </p>
                {nameUpdated && <p class="settings-success" role="status">Your name is saved.</p>}
                {nameError && (
                  <p class="settings-error" role="alert">
                    That did not save. Nothing has changed; try again, and if it keeps failing, contact{' '}
                    <a href="mailto:ryan@tokenstoagents.ai">ryan@tokenstoagents.ai</a>.
                  </p>
                )}
                <form class="settings-form" method="POST" action={nameAction}>
                  <div class="field">
                    <label class="field-label" for="settings-first-name">First name</label>
                    <input class="field-input" id="settings-first-name" type="text" name="firstName" maxlength="120" value={name?.firstName ?? ''} />
                  </div>
                  <div class="field">
                    <label class="field-label" for="settings-last-name">Last name</label>
                    <input class="field-input" id="settings-last-name" type="text" name="lastName" maxlength="120" value={name?.lastName ?? ''} />
                  </div>
                  <button class="field-submit" type="submit">Save name</button>
                </form>
              </AccountRow>

              <AccountRow label="Email" value={email ?? 'none on file'} open={emailRowOpen}>
                <p class="settings-panel-line">
                  Changing it takes two confirmations, both by email: one to this address, approving the
                  request, then one to the new address, proving you can receive mail there. Nothing about your
                  account changes until both are done.
                </p>
                {emailRequested && (
                  <p class="settings-success" role="status">
                    A confirmation is on its way to {email ?? 'your current address'}. Open it to continue;
                    ignore it and nothing changes.
                  </p>
                )}
                {emailError && (
                  <p class="settings-error" role="alert">
                    {EMAIL_ERROR_MESSAGES[emailError] ?? 'That did not go through. Nothing has changed.'}
                  </p>
                )}
                <form class="settings-form" method="POST" action={emailAction}>
                  <div class="field">
                    <label class="field-label" for="settings-new-email">New email address</label>
                    <input class="field-input" id="settings-new-email" type="email" name="newEmail" required maxlength="320" />
                  </div>
                  <button class="field-submit" type="submit">Request the change</button>
                </form>
              </AccountRow>

              <AccountRow label="Resumé email" value={resumeEmailValue} open={resumeEmailRowOpen}>
                <p class="settings-panel-line">
                  The email that shows on your resumés and cover letters. Separate from your login, so you can
                  put a different address on what you send out.
                </p>
                {resumeEmailUpdated && <p class="settings-success" role="status">Saved.</p>}
                {resumeEmailError && (
                  <p class="settings-error" role="alert">That does not look like an email address. Nothing has changed.</p>
                )}
                <form class="settings-form" method="POST" action={resumeEmailAction}>
                  <div class="field field-checkbox">
                    <label class="field-checkbox-label" for="settings-resume-email-use-login">
                      <input class="field-checkbox-input" id="settings-resume-email-use-login" type="checkbox" name="resumeEmailUseLogin" checked={resumeEmail.useLogin} />
                      Use my login email on my resumés
                    </label>
                  </div>
                  <div class="field">
                    <label class="field-label" for="settings-resume-email">Custom resumé email</label>
                    <input class="field-input" id="settings-resume-email" type="email" name="resumeEmail" maxlength="320" value={resumeEmail.custom ?? ''} />
                    <p class="field-hint">
                      {resumeEmail.custom !== null
                        ? 'Using your custom email again. Edit it or clear it anytime.'
                        : 'The email that shows on your resumés. Your login stays what it is.'}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <button class="field-submit" type="submit">Save</button>
                </form>
              </AccountRow>

              <AccountRow label="Handle" value={handleValue} open={handleRowOpen}>
                <p class="settings-panel-line">
                  Reserves /u/{handle ?? 'your-handle'} for a public profile page. This run keeps every
                  classification above private dark, so this is a private preview only you can open, not a
                  public page anyone else can reach yet.
                </p>
                <p class="settings-panel-line">
                  {HANDLE_MIN_LENGTH} to {HANDLE_MAX_LENGTH} characters: lowercase letters, numbers and
                  hyphens only, starting and ending with a letter or number. Leave it blank and save to give
                  the handle up.
                </p>
                {handleUpdated && <p class="settings-success" role="status">Your handle is saved.</p>}
                {handleCleared && <p class="settings-success" role="status">Your handle is cleared.</p>}
                {handleError && (
                  <p class="settings-error" role="alert">
                    {HANDLE_ERROR_MESSAGES[handleError] ?? 'That did not save. Nothing has changed.'}
                  </p>
                )}
                {handle && (
                  <p class="settings-panel-line">
                    <a class="settings-link" href={withBase(`/u/${handle}`)}>Preview /u/{handle}</a>{' '}
                    (only you can open it, this run).
                  </p>
                )}
                <form class="settings-form" method="POST" action={handleAction}>
                  <div class="field">
                    <label class="field-label" for="settings-handle">Handle</label>
                    <input class="field-input" id="settings-handle" type="text" name="handle" maxlength={HANDLE_MAX_LENGTH} autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" value={handle ?? ''} placeholder="ryan-payne" />
                  </div>
                  <button class="field-submit" type="submit">Save handle</button>
                </form>
              </AccountRow>
            </Panel>

            {paidViewer && (
            <Panel title="Models and keys" class="settings-panel">
              <span slot="aside" class="models-aside">
                Your key, your bill · encrypted for you alone, read only at drafting time
              </span>

              <div id="keys" class="keys-anchor" />

              {
                !byokOn ? (
                  <p class="keys-note">
                    Bring-your-own-key generation is turned off for this deployment right now. Nothing here has
                    been lost: this is a feature switch, not a fault, and no key can be added, replaced, or
                    removed while it is off.
                  </p>
                ) : !keysConfigured ? (
                  <p class="keys-note">
                    Key storage is not configured on this deployment. The encryption secret this page needs to
                    seal a key before storing it is not set, so adding, replacing, or removing a key is not
                    possible right now. Nothing has been lost: no key has been read or written. This is an
                    operator setting, not something you can fix from this page.
                  </p>
                ) : (
                  <ProviderRows
                    rows={providerRows}
                    modelAction={modelAction}
                    keysSaveAction={keysSaveAction}
                    keysRemoveAction={keysRemoveAction}
                    modelUpdated={modelUpdated}
                    modelError={modelError}
                    settingsPath={settingsPath}
                    openModel={openModel}
                    openKey={openKey}
                  />
                )
              }

              {hasDraftSpend && (
                <p class="keys-note keys-spend">
                  Drafting spend so far: {draftSpendText} across {draftCount} {draftCount === 1 ? 'draft' : 'drafts'} on your key, {draftTokensText} tokens. Estimated, prices as of {PRICES_AS_OF}.
                </p>
              )}

              <div class="drafting-toggle">
                {generationUpdated && <p class="settings-success" role="status">Saved.</p>}
                {generationError && (
                  <p class="settings-error" role="alert">
                    That did not save. Nothing has changed; try again, and if it keeps failing, contact{' '}
                    <a href="mailto:ryan@tokenstoagents.ai">ryan@tokenstoagents.ai</a>.
                  </p>
                )}
                <form class="settings-form drafting-form" method="POST" action={generationAction}>
                  <label class="drafting-label" for="settings-generate-on-apply">
                    <input
                      class="field-checkbox-input"
                      id="settings-generate-on-apply"
                      type="checkbox"
                      name="generateOnApply"
                      checked={generateOnApply}
                    />
                    <span class="drafting-copy">
                      <span class="drafting-copy-main">Draft a resumé and cover letter each time I apply.</span>{' '}
                      <span class="drafting-copy-aside">
                        Drafting starts in the background; by the time you are done applying, the draft is
                        waiting.
                        {connectedKeys.length === 0
                          ? ' Paused until you connect a key above.'
                          : soleWritingModel
                            ? ` Uses your ${soleWritingModel.writingLabel} on ${soleWritingModel.name}.`
                            : ' Uses the writing model you chose for each connected key.'}
                      </span>
                    </span>
                  </label>
                  <button class="field-submit" type="submit">Save</button>
                </form>
              </div>
            </Panel>
            )}

            <Panel title="Your data" class="settings-panel">
              <p class="settings-panel-line">
                Two things here: download a copy of everything on file about you, or delete your account and
                everything in it.
              </p>

              {deleteFailed && (
                <p class="settings-error" role="alert">
                  The delete did not complete. Nothing has been reported as removed that was not actually
                  removed; your account is unchanged. Try again, and if it keeps failing, contact{' '}
                  <a href="mailto:ryan@tokenstoagents.ai">ryan@tokenstoagents.ai</a>.
                </p>
              )}

              <a class="account-button" href={exportHref}>Download your data</a>
              <p class="keys-note keys-note-quiet">It's a short file. That's the point.</p>

              <details class="delete-disclosure" id="delete-disclosure">
                <summary class="delete-summary">Delete your account</summary>
                <div class="delete-body">
                  <p class="settings-panel-line">This erases, permanently and with no undo:</p>
                  <ul class="delete-list">
                    <li>Your identity: name, email, and the fact that your address is verified.</li>
                    <li>Your sign-in history and every active session, on every device.</li>
                    <li>Your credential row and any lingering password-reset request.</li>
                    <li>Your entitlement record: your tier and how you signed up.</li>
                  </ul>
                  <p class="settings-panel-line">This does not, and cannot, reach:</p>
                  <ul class="delete-list">
                    <li>
                      A mailing-list subscription with beehiiv, if you have one. It is a separate identity
                      with no link back to this account; cancel it from the link in any newsletter email.
                    </li>
                    <li>Delivery logs for email this site has already sent you, which live in Resend's own systems.</li>
                  </ul>
                  <form class="delete-form" method="POST" action={deleteAction}>
                    <label class="delete-confirm-label" for="delete-confirm">
                      Type DELETE to confirm.
                    </label>
                    <input
                      class="field-input"
                      id="delete-confirm"
                      name="confirm"
                      type="text"
                      autocomplete="off"
                      required
                      pattern="DELETE"
                    />
                    <div class="delete-actions">
                      <button class="account-button account-button-destructive" type="submit">
                        Yes, delete my account
                      </button>
                      <button class="account-button-quiet" type="button" id="cancel-delete">
                        Cancel
                      </button>
                    </div>
                  </form>
                </div>
              </details>
            </Panel>

            <div class="settings-back">
              <a class="settings-link" href={profileHref}>View your profile</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h1>Not available</h1>
            {reason === 'email-unverified' ? (
              <>
                <p class="muted">Confirm your email and this page opens.</p>
                <div class="account-links">
                  <a class="account-link" href={withBase('/verify-email')}>Resend the link</a>
                </div>
              </>
            ) : (
              <>
                <p class="muted">Sign in to manage your settings.</p>
                <div class="account-links">
                  <a class="account-link" href={withBase('/sign-in')}>Sign in</a>
                  <a class="account-link" href={withBase('/sign-up')}>No account yet? Create one.</a>
                </div>
              </>
            )}
          </>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Progressive enhancement only. Without this, "Cancel" is inert and the
  // disclosure still closes the same way it opened: click the summary again,
  // or move focus away. Nothing on this page depends on this script running.
  const cancelButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#cancel-delete');
  const disclosure = document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('#delete-disclosure');
  const summary = disclosure?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('summary');

  cancelButton?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (disclosure) disclosure.open = false;
    summary?.focus();
  });
</script>

